            <div xml:id="d284">

                <pb facs="0382" n="274" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg274"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/8501: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-04-01T14:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 1, 1927—2
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 1—7:06
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>314. Following from American consul general, Hankow, has been repeated to
                    commander in chief: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“March 31, 3 p.m. Requested that naval forces be augmented, passenger
                            ships to be convoyed through to Shanghai. Many American[s] refusing to
                            leave without such convoy.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
